+# Typewriter Blog API — Environment Variables
+#
+# Posts live in a separate private GitHub repo of markdown files. This service
+# keeps a working clone, indexes it in memory, and follows pushes. There is no
+# database.
+
+# ── Server ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
+PORT=8081
+# Comma-separated. Must include the exact origin the frontend is served from.
+ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,https://blogs.madhavapoojari.fyi
+
+# ── Auth ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+JWT_SECRET=change-me-to-a-strong-random-secret
+ADMIN_USERNAME=madhava-poojari
+# Generate with:  ./server hashpw 'your-password'
+# The plaintext password is never stored or read from the environment.
+ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH=
+
+# ── Content repo ────────────────────────────────────────────
+# Must be PRIVATE: `visibility: private` only means something if the repo is.
+CONTENT_REPO_URL=git@github.com:madhav-poojari/blog-content.git
+# Server-owned, disposable. Safe to delete at any time; it is re-cloned.
+CONTENT_REPO_PATH=/var/lib/blog-content
+CONTENT_REPO_BRANCH=main
+# Deploy key with WRITE access (needed to push generated frontmatter).
+CONTENT_SSH_KEY_PATH=/etc/blog-engine/deploy_key
+# Identity for frontmatter commits. Commits by this address are excluded when
+# computing a post's "updated" time, so a normalize sweep does not look like an
+# edit to every post.
+CONTENT_BOT_NAME=blog-engine-bot
+CONTENT_BOT_EMAIL=bot@blog-engine.local
+
+# ── Sync ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+# Shared secret configured on the GitHub webhook (Settings → Webhooks).
+GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
+# Fallback for missed webhooks. Cheap: one `git ls-remote` per tick.
+SYNC_POLL_INTERVAL=5m
+# Local time. The one moment per day that writes frontmatter back to the repo.
+SYNC_DAILY_SWEEP_AT=03:00
+# true writes frontmatter back on every push instead of once a day. Leave false
+# unless waiting a day for files to become self-describing bothers you; posts
+# are served with full metadata immediately either way.
+NORMALIZE_ON_EVERY_SYNC=false
+# Directory names that should not become tags.
+IGNORED_PATH_TAGS=uncategorised
+
+# ── Image storage (optional) ────────────────────────────────
+# Only needed for the upload endpoint. Images referenced by absolute URL in
+# markdown need none of this.
+S3_ENDPOINT=https://<account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
+S3_REGION=auto
+S3_BUCKET=blog-images
+S3_ACCESS_KEY=
+S3_SECRET_KEY=
+# The domain uploads are actually served from. Required for R2: without it the
+# API returns an amazonaws.com URL that does not resolve.
+S3_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://cdn.madhavapoojari.fyi
